      "scenario": "The newly pinned legacy script runs docker rm under set -e before rm -rf \"$work\" in its EXIT trap. If Docker cleanup fails, Bash aborts the trap and never removes the host temporary directory. Running the unchanged full script with a local Docker fault injector (start returns 7, rm returns 9) exits 9 and leaves its root. A paired control with the same start failure but rm success exits 7 and leaves TMPDIR empty. No Docker daemon, real container or network is used. This is a pre-existing trap defect exposed by review of the newly adopted pin, rather than a shell-parser bypass.",
